      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV global series",
          "heading": "Ireland Women secure victory against Japan following resilient second-half display",
          "body": "Ireland Women bounced back from their opening defeat to the USA by registering a 31-24 win over Japan at Dexcom Stadium. After racing into an early 19-0 lead through Brittany Hogan and Beibhinn Parsons, Ireland withstood a spirited Japanese comeback. Parsons, who scored twice, claimed the record as Ireland’s all-time leading try scorer. Coach Scott Bemand praised his side's improved response, noting that the victory was crucial for momentum as the team looks ahead to their upcoming matches outside the WXV Series."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
