          "heading": "Welsh Players Impress As Cardiff Defeats Scarlets In URC Opener",
          "body": "Cardiff secured a hard-fought victory over Scarlets in the opening round of the United Rugby Championship, with number eight Taine Basham earning player of the match honours. While the derby was described by head coach Corniel van Zyl as an underwhelming occasion, standout moments included Blair Murray’s solo try for the Scarlets and Callum Sheedy’s audacious header. Elsewhere, Welsh exports Dewi Lake and Jac Morgan made strong impressions for Gloucester during the opening weekend of the English Premiership."
