      "edition": "Tuesday 29 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV Global Series",
          "heading": "Sakura XV show attacking promise despite defeat to Ireland side",
          "body": "The Sakura XV fell to a 24-31 defeat against Ireland in Galway, marking their third consecutive loss. Despite a slow start that saw them trail 19-0, the team rallied with a more physical approach and two tries from Moe Nagaoka. Head coach Toshizumi Kitagawa praised the side's improved linespeed and set-piece performance in the second half. While the result did not go their way, Kitagawa noted, \"I told the girls to trust themselves in these games, as we are playing against a team ranked higher.\""
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugby Asia 247"
      }
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-09-29",
