      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection crisis",
          "heading": "Australia faces midfield injury concerns ahead of upcoming Bledisloe Cup showdown",
          "body": "The Wallabies could be without their starting midfield for the Bledisloe Cup match against the All Blacks. Len Ikitau has sustained an ankle injury, while Hunter Paisami faces a hearing with the SANZAAR Foul Play Review Committee today following a citation from the victory over South Africa. Head coach Les Kiss noted the team is being precautionary with Ikitau’s ankle. Meanwhile, the Wallabies are evaluating whether to move Joseph-Aukuso Sua'ali'i into the centres or use him as a fullback option."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland Women defeat Japan 31-24 in Galway",
          "body": ""
        }
      ],
