      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-09-29",
      "edition": "Tuesday 29 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Wallabies test",
          "heading": "Australia proves resilience as South Africa reflects on Perth defeat",
          "body": "While South Africa’s recent defeat in Perth has sparked discussion, observers note the result serves as a reminder that Australia remains a formidable opponent under Les Kiss. The Wallabies, currently on a six-match unbeaten streak, capitalised on a heavily rotated Springboks side to secure a 42-38 victory. The result lifted Australia to sixth in the World Rugby rankings, with analysts viewing the performance as a genuine 'statement' victory as nations continue to build depth ahead of next year’s World Cup."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland Women defeat Japan 31-24 in Galway",
